narratives.Overview:
## Summary

`deft update` (and `directive init`) re-project a Directive-owned `.claude/settings.json` on every upgrade (per the "Agent-host direct-write hooks" feature, #2438 / #2596). For a consumer repo that deliberately does **not** want the fail-closed Claude Code hook, there is no persistent opt-out: removing the file is treated as drift and silently re-created by the next `deft update`. Combined with how the Claude Code `PreToolUse` gate behaves in practice, this produced real friction for a repo that uses Claude Code as a dev/agent host but not the interactive session-ritual workflow.

Reporting from a consumer deposit on **`@deftai/directive` 0.80.0** (dogfooding a separate project).

## What happened

Upgrading a consumer repo's vendored `.deft/core` from 0.75.0 → 0.80.0 projected `.claude/settings.json` (plus `.codex`/`.cursor`/`.grok` equivalents). The Claude `PreToolUse` gate then:

1. **Blocked every `Edit`/`Write`** until a gated `deft session:start` + `deft doctor` ritual was recorded — expected per design, but this repo's workflow doesn't run that ritual, so it was pure friction.
2. **Gated edits to files _outside_ the repo too.** Claude Code's `PreToolUse` matcher keys on the *tool name* (`Edit|Write|…`), not the target path, so once the hook is loaded for the session it fail-closes on edits to any path — e.g. it blocked edits to files in a different directory entirely (agent memory files under `~/.claude/...`).
3. **Went stale on every `git` HEAD change.** The compact/HEAD re-arm (#2113) marks the ritual stale; a routine merge+pull mid-session re-blocked all writes until `deft session:start` was re-run. In a repo with a normal PR cadence this fires constantly.
4. **Survived deletion.** After removing `.claude/settings.json` on purpose, the docs' own guidance ("Repair missing/drifted entries: `deft update`") means the next upgrade re-adds it — the removal isn't honored as intent.

Net effect: to do ordinary work in the repo after the upgrade, every session needs `deft session:start && deft doctor` before the first edit, re-run after each HEAD change — and a deliberate removal doesn't stick.

## Why this is a problem for this class of repo

Not every repo that has Claude Code available runs the Directive interactive session-ritual + active-xBRIEF workflow. A benchmark harness / library / CI-style repo may use Claude Code purely as a coding host and never adopt the ritual gate. For those, the projected fail-closed hook is a net negative, and the lack of a durable opt-out means it keeps coming back.

## Requests

1. **A persistent, documented opt-out** so a consumer who doesn't want a given host's hooks isn't overridden by the next `deft update` — e.g. a `plan.policy` field (`hostHooks: { claude: false, … }`) or a deposit-local ignore list that `deft update` honors instead of treating an absent/edited file as drift-to-repair.
2. **Honor intentional removal**: distinguish "deleted on purpose" from "drifted / partial" so `deft update` doesn't silently re-project a host file the operator removed.
3. **(Consider)** narrowing or documenting the path-scope limitation — because the Claude `PreToolUse` matcher is tool-name-based, the gate applies to writes anywhere the session touches, including outside the project root. At minimum this is worth an explicit note in the "Agent-host direct-write hooks" docs.

## Reference: the projected `.claude/settings.json` (0.80.0)

```json
{
  "hooks": {
    "SessionStart": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "deft hook:dispatch --host claude --event session.start",
            "timeout": 5
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "PreToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "Edit|Write|WriteFile|CreateFile|MultiEdit|NotebookEdit|StrReplace|SearchReplace|Delete|DeleteFile|ApplyPatch|apply_patch",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "deft hook:dispatch --host claude --event tool.before",
            "timeout": 5
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "Task|SubagentStart|spawn_subagent|start_agent|CreateAgent",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "deft hook:dispatch --host claude --event tool.before",
            "timeout": 5
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "PreCompact": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "deft hook:dispatch --host claude --event session.compact",
            "timeout": 5
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "PostCompact": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "deft hook:dispatch --host claude --event session.compact",
            "timeout": 5
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

Docs: `.deft/core/commands.md` § "Agent-host direct-write hooks (#2438, #2596)".
